nd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">one shoe had a hole in it</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">the shoes were brand new</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">he shoes were too dirty</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">the stitching on the shoes was broken</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4},{"id":"en-c19-t2-l-g3-2","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 29-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span>Why did the project to make ‘new’ shoes out of old shoes fail?</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>People believed the 'new' pairs of shoes were unhygienic.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>There were not enough good parts to use in the old shoes.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>The shoes in the ‘new’ pairs were not completely alike.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span>Bella and Don agree that they can present their topic</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>from a new angle.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>with relevant images.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>in a straightforward way.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":2}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/cambridge-ielts-19-academic-listening-2-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c19-t2-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/158823-cambridge-ielts-19-academic-listening-2-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c19-t2-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"diagram_labelling","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer.</p><p><strong>Tardigrades</strong></p><p>- more than 1,000 species, 0.05–1.2 millimetres long</p><p>- also known as water ‘bears’ (due to how they <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>) and ‘moss piglets’</p><p><strong>Physical appearance</strong></p><p>- a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> round body and four pairs of legs</p><p>- claws or <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> for gripping</p><p>- absence of respiratory organs</p><p>- body filled with a liquid that carries both <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and blood</p><p>- mouth shaped like a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> with teeth called stylets</p><p><strong>Habitat</strong></p><p>- often found at the bottom of a lake or on plants</p><p>- very resilient and can exist in very low or high <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p><strong>Cryptobiosis</strong></p><p>- In dry conditions, they roll into a ball called a ‘tun’.</p><p>- They stay alive with a much lower metabolism than usual.</p><p>- A type of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> ensures their DNA is not damaged.</p><p>- Research is underway to find out how many days they can stay alive in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p><strong>Feeding</strong></p><p>- consume liquids, e.g., those found in moss or <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>- may eat other tardigrades</p><p><strong>Conservation status</strong></p><p>- They are not considered to be <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c19-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/cambridge-ielts-19-academic-listening-2-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c19-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-c19-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"MATHIESON","correct_answer_variants":["MATHIESON"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_154254_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c19-t2-l-q2","part_id":"en-c19-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"beginners","correct_answer_variants":["beginners"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_154254_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c19-t2-l-q3","part_id":"en-c19-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"college","correct_answer_variants":["college"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_154254_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c19-t2-l-q4","part_id":"en-c19-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c19-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","corr